    {"id":"phrasal-verbs","title":"Phrasal verbs","about":"look up, give up, put off … — from the Russian to the verb.","ask":"translate","units":[137,145], "entries": [
      {"id":"get-on","en":"get on","ru":"садиться (в автобус, поезд)","ex":"The bus was full. We couldn’t get on.","unit":137},
      {"id":"drive-off","en":"drive off","ru":"уехать (на машине)","ex":"A woman got into the car and drove off.","unit":137},
      {"id":"come-back","en":"come back","ru":"вернуться","ex":"Sarah is leaving tomorrow and coming back on Saturday.","unit":137},
      {"id":"turn-round","en":"turn round","ru":"обернуться, развернуться","alt":["turn around"],"ex":"When I touched him on the shoulder, he turned round.","unit":137},
      {"id":"break-down","en":"break down","ru":"сломаться (о машине, технике)","ex":"Sorry I’m late. The car broke down.","unit":137},
      {"id":"find-out","en":"find out","ru":"выяснить, узнать","ex":"I never found out who sent me the flowers.","unit":137},
      {"id":"take-off","en":"take off","ru":"взлететь (о самолёте)","ex":"I was nervous as the plane took off.","unit":137},
      {"id":"give-up","en":"give up","ru":"сдаться; бросить (занятие)","ex":"I tried many times to contact her. In the end I gave up.","unit":137},
      {"id":"get-by","en":"get by","ru":"обходиться, справляться (с малым)","ex":"My French isn’t good, but it’s enough to get by.","unit":137},
      {"id":"run-away","en":"run away","ru":"убегать","ex":"Why did you run away from me?","unit":137},
      {"id":"keep-up-with","en":"keep up with","ru":"поспевать за, не отставать от","ex":"You’re walking too fast. I can’t keep up with you.","unit":137},
      {"id":"look-forward-to","en":"look forward to","ru":"ждать с нетерпением","ex":"Are you looking forward to your trip?","unit":137},
      {"id":"wake-up","en":"wake up","ru":"проснуться; разбудить","ex":"The baby is asleep. Don’t wake her up.","unit":137},
      {"id":"throw-away","en":"throw away","ru":"выбросить","ex":"I want to keep this box, so don’t throw it away.","unit":137},
      {"id":"get-in","en":"get in","ru":"войти, забраться внутрь","ex":"How did the thieves get in?","unit":138},
      {"id":"get-out","en":"get out","ru":"выйти, выбраться","ex":"Stay in the car. Don’t get out.","unit":138},
      {"id":"move-in","en":"move in","ru":"въехать (в новое жильё)","ex":"I’ve got a new apartment. I’m moving in on Friday.","unit":138},
      {"id":"move-out","en":"move out","ru":"съехать (с квартиры)","ex":"We moved out of our flat last month.","unit":138},
      {"id":"check-in","en":"check in","ru":"зарегистрироваться (в гостинице, аэропорту)","ex":"As soon as I got to the airport, I checked in.","unit":138},
      {"id":"check-out","en":"check out","ru":"выписаться (из гостиницы)","ex":"We paid the hotel bill and checked out.","unit":138},
      {"id":"drop-in","en":"drop in","ru":"заглянуть, зайти (без предупреждения)","ex":"I dropped in to see Chris on my way home.","unit":138},
      {"id":"join-in","en":"join in","ru":"присоединиться (к тому, что уже идёт)","ex":"They were playing cards, so I joined in.","unit":138},
      {"id":"plug-in","en":"plug in","ru":"включить в розетку","ex":"The fridge isn’t working because you haven’t plugged it in.","unit":138},
      {"id":"take-in","en":"take in","ru":"обмануть","ex":"The man said he was a policeman and I believed him. I was completely taken in.","unit":138},
      {"id":"fill-in","en":"fill in","ru":"заполнить (анкету, бланк)","alt":["fill out"],"ex":"Please fill in the application form.","unit":138},
      {"id":"eat-out","en":"eat out","ru":"поесть в ресторане, не дома","ex":"There wasn’t anything to eat at home, so we decided to eat out.","unit":138},
      {"id":"drop-out","en":"drop out","ru":"бросить (учёбу, курс)","ex":"Gary went to university but dropped out after a year.","unit":138},
      {"id":"get-out-of","en":"get out of","ru":"отвертеться, отделаться от","ex":"I promised I’d go to the wedding. I can’t get out of it now.","unit":138},
      {"id":"leave-out","en":"leave out","ru":"пропустить, не включить","ex":"You can leave out the word ‘that’.","unit":138},
      {"id":"cross-out","en":"cross out","ru":"вычеркнуть","ex":"Some of the names on the list had been crossed out.","unit":138},
      {"id":"go-out","en":"go out","ru":"погаснуть (о свете, огне)","ex":"Suddenly all the lights in the building went out.","unit":139},
      {"id":"put-out","en":"put out","ru":"потушить (огонь, сигарету)","ex":"I put the fire out with a fire extinguisher.","unit":139},
      {"id":"blow-out","en":"blow out","ru":"задуть (свечу)","ex":"We don’t need the candle. You can blow it out.","unit":139},
      {"id":"work-out","en":"work out","ru":"тренироваться, заниматься спортом","ex":"Rachel works out at the gym three times a week.","unit":139},
      {"id":"work-out-2","en":"work out","ru":"понять, разобраться; вычислить","alt":["figure out"],"ex":"Investigators are trying to work out what caused the accident.","unit":139},
      {"id":"carry-out","en":"carry out","ru":"выполнять, проводить (приказ, опыт, исследование)","ex":"An investigation into the accident will be carried out.","unit":139},
      {"id":"give-out","en":"give out","ru":"раздавать","alt":["hand out"],"ex":"At the end of the lecture, the speaker gave out information sheets.","unit":139},
      {"id":"point-out","en":"point out","ru":"указать, обратить внимание (на)","ex":"I didn’t realise I’d made a mistake until somebody pointed it out to me.","unit":139},
      {"id":"run-out-of","en":"run out of","ru":"израсходовать всё, остаться без","ex":"We ran out of petrol on the motorway.","unit":139},
      {"id":"sort-out","en":"sort out","ru":"уладить, разобраться; привести в порядок","ex":"There are a few problems we need to sort out.","unit":139},
      {"id":"turn-out","en":"turn out","ru":"оказаться (в итоге)","ex":"Nobody believed Paul at first, but he turned out to be right.","unit":139},
      {"id":"try-out","en":"try out","ru":"опробовать, испытать","ex":"The company is trying out some new software at the moment.","unit":139},
      {"id":"turn-on","en":"turn on","ru":"включить","alt":["switch on"],"ex":"It’s dark in here. Can you turn the light on?","unit":140},
      {"id":"turn-off","en":"turn off","ru":"выключить","alt":["switch off"],"ex":"Shall I leave the lights on or turn them off?","unit":140},
      {"id":"go-on","en":"go on","ru":"происходить","ex":"What’s all that noise? What’s going on?","unit":140},
      {"id":"call-off","en":"call off","ru":"отменить","ex":"The concert had to be called off because of the weather.","unit":140},
      {"id":"put-off","en":"put off","ru":"откладывать","ex":"We can’t put off making a decision. We have to decide now.","unit":140},
      {"id":"put-on","en":"put on","ru":"надеть","ex":"My hands were cold, so I put my gloves on.","unit":140},
      {"id":"take-off-2","en":"take off","ru":"снять (одежду, очки)","ex":"It was warm, so I took off my coat.","unit":140},
      {"id":"put-on-weight","en":"put on weight","ru":"набрать вес, поправиться","ex":"I’ve put on two kilos in the last month.","unit":140},
      {"id":"try-on","en":"try on","ru":"примерить","ex":"I tried on a jacket in the shop, but it didn’t look right.","unit":140},
      {"id":"set-off","en":"set off","ru":"отправиться (в путь)","ex":"We set off early to avoid the traffic.","unit":140},
      {"id":"see-off","en":"see off","ru":"провожать","ex":"We went to the station with her to see her off.","unit":140},
      {"id":"carry-on","en":"carry on","ru":"продолжать (делать что-то)","alt":["go on"],"ex":"I don’t want to carry on working here.","unit":141},
      {"id":"keep-on","en":"keep on","ru":"всё время, снова и снова (делать что-то)","ex":"He keeps on criticising me. It’s not fair!","unit":141},
      {"id":"get-on-2","en":"get on","ru":"продвигаться, справляться (How are you …?)","ex":"How are you getting on in your new job?","unit":141},
      {"id":"get-on-with","en":"get on with","ru":"ладить (с кем-то)","ex":"Richard gets on well with his neighbours.","unit":141},
      {"id":"get-on-with-2","en":"get on with","ru":"продолжить (работу) после перерыва","ex":"I must get on with my work. I have a lot to do.","unit":141},
      {"id":"doze-off","en":"doze off","ru":"задремать","alt":["drop off","nod off"],"ex":"I dozed off during the lecture. It was very boring.","unit":141},
      {"id":"finish-off","en":"finish off","ru":"доделать, закончить","ex":"Nearly. I’ll finish it off tomorrow.","unit":141},
      {"id":"go-off","en":"go off","ru":"сработать, зазвонить (о будильнике, сигнализации)","ex":"Did you hear the alarm go off?","unit":141},
      {"id":"put-off-2","en":"put off","ru":"отбить охоту, оттолкнуть","ex":"We wanted to go to the exhibition, but we were put off by the long queue.","unit":141},
      {"id":"rip-off","en":"rip off","ru":"обобрать, обмануть (с ценой)","ex":"You paid £2,000 for that painting? I think you were ripped off.","unit":141},
      {"id":"show-off","en":"show off","ru":"хвастаться, красоваться","ex":"Look at that boy riding with no hands. He’s just showing off.","unit":141},
      {"id":"tell-off","en":"tell off","ru":"отругать","ex":"Clare’s mother told her off for wearing dirty shoes in the house.","unit":141},
      {"id":"put-up","en":"put up","ru":"повесить (на стену)","ex":"I put a picture up on the wall.","unit":142},
      {"id":"take-down","en":"take down","ru":"снять (со стены)","ex":"I didn’t like the picture, so I took it down.","unit":142},
